  "schema": "dreal005.a4_geometry_identity.v2",
  "issue": 15,
  "requirement": "A4 must verify geometry identity from what GitHub serves: the delivered final_aircraft must be the aircraft that really ran in the solver cases.",
  "method": {
    "leg_1_regeneration": "x12 is read from the delivered manifest, the solver geometry is rebuilt through the same frozen code path (build_geometry -> prepare_case) and the resulting .vspgeom sha256 must equal the geometry_sha256 that plan.json recorded for the paid case. VSPAERO is only ever given the .vspgeom, so an equal .vspgeom means the solver flew the delivered aircraft.",
    "leg_2_canonical_xml": "the delivered .vsp3 and the case .vsp3 are compared element by element with OpenVSP element IDs masked. IDs are re-randomised on every import/export (measured: 1,703 of 2,468 lines differ between the two files and every one of them is an <ID>/AttachID value), so raw byte equality is impossible by construction and would be a false test.",
    "disclosed_residuals": "the delivered files are exported with OpenVSP default tessellation, while each paid case was written with tess_u=12/tess_w=25; that shows up as Tess_U/Tess_W/MaxGrowth differences and is reported per pair as non_geometric_differences instead of being suppressed.",
    "no_solver": "neither leg starts a solver; leg 1 writes with StopBeforeRun=1, physical_solver_starts 0."
  },
